# GNU General Public License (GPL) Version 3 Summary

The GNU GPL v3 is a **free, copyleft license** designed to guarantee users the freedom to share and change all versions of a program. It ensures software remains free for all users, regardless of whether it is distributed for a fee or gratis.

## 1. Core Definitions
*   **The Program:** Any copyrightable work licensed under the GPL.
*   **Modify:** To copy from or adapt all or part of the work in a way requiring copyright permission.
*   **Convey:** Any propagation that enables other parties to make or receive copies (excluding mere network interaction).
*   **Corresponding Source:** All source code needed to generate, install, and run the object code, including scripts to control those activities. It excludes "System Libraries."

## 2. Key Requirements for Distribution
If you distribute (convey) the software, you must adhere to the following:

### Verbatim Copies (Section 4)
*   Must include an appropriate copyright notice.
*   Must keep all "no warranty" notices intact.
*   Must provide a copy of this License to the recipient.

### Modified Source Versions (Section 5)
*   **Notice:** Must carry prominent notices stating you modified it and the date.
*   **Licensing:** The entire work must be licensed under GPL v3 as a whole.
*   **Interfaces:** If the program has interactive user interfaces, they must display "Appropriate Legal Notices."

### Non-Source Forms / Object Code (Section 6)
To convey object code, you must also provide the **Corresponding Source** via:
*   A physical medium.
*   A written offer (valid for 3+ years) to provide the source.
*   Access from a designated network server at no charge.

## 3. User Protections & Anti-Circumvention
*   **Anti-Tivoization:** If a "User Product" (consumer device) uses the software, the distributor must provide **Installation Information** (keys/methods) so the user can install modified versions of the software.
*   **Legal Rights:** No covered work shall be deemed part of an "effective technological measure" under anti-circumvention laws (like the WIPO treaty). By licensing under GPL, authors waive the power to forbid circumvention of such measures.

## 4. Patents & Licensing
*   **Automatic License:** Each contributor grants a non-exclusive, worldwide, royalty-free patent license to users.
*   **No Further Restrictions:** You cannot impose additional fees, royalties, or litigation restrictions (like patent lawsuits) on the exercise of rights granted by the license.
*   **Discriminatory Agreements:** You cannot enter into patent deals with third parties that discriminate against specific recipients of the software.

## 5. Termination & Reinstatement (Section 8)
Violating the license automatically terminates your rights. However, rights can be reinstated:
*   **Provisionally:** If you cease all violations.
*   **Permanently:** If the copyright holder doesn't notify you within 60 days of cessation, or if you fix the violation within 30 days of your first-ever notice of violation.

## 6. Important Legal Disclaimers

### No Warranty
> "THERE IS NO WARRANTY FOR THE PROGRAM, TO THE EXTENT PERMITTED BY APPLICABLE LAW... THE ENTIRE RISK AS TO THE QUALITY AND PERFORMANCE OF THE PROGRAM IS WITH YOU."

### Limitation of Liability
> "IN NO EVENT... WILL ANY COPYRIGHT HOLDER... BE LIABLE TO YOU FOR DAMAGES, INCLUDING ANY GENERAL, SPECIAL, INCIDENTAL OR CONSEQUENTIAL DAMAGES ARISING OUT OF THE USE OR INABILITY TO USE THE PROGRAM."

## 7. Implementation Guide
To apply GPL v3 to a new program, developers should attach the following notice to every source file:

```text
Copyright (C) <year> <name of author>

This program is free software: you can redistribute it and/or modify
it under the terms of the GNU General Public License as published by
the Free Software Foundation, either version 3 of the License, or
(at your option) any later version.

This program is distributed in the hope that it will be useful,
but WITHOUT ANY WARRANTY; without even the implied warranty of
MERCHANTABILITY or FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE. See the
GNU General Public License for more details.

You should have received a copy of the GNU General Public License
along with this program. If not, see <https://www.gnu.org/licenses/>.
```

### Additional Notes
*   **Affero GPL (AGPL):** GPL v3 allows linking with works under the GNU Affero General Public License v3.
*   **Proprietary Linking:** GPL does **not** permit incorporating the program into proprietary programs. For libraries that need to link with proprietary apps, the **GNU Lesser General Public License (LGPL)** is recommended.
